      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DABNEY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case concerns how far the Federal Circuit can properly go in taking jurisdiction to the exclusion of the regional circuits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, Congress did want patent law to be uniform, didn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Dabney, has the Federal Circuit held that whenever there's a patent claim in a -- in a -- a patent issue in a counterclaim, it has jurisdiction? Or must it be a compulsory counterclaim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "need look hardly beyond 486 U.S., page 814. Right then and there the Court was faced with the question, how do we know if a case properly belongs in the Federal Circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a preliminary injunction that was issued in January of 2000, which remains in effect to this day upon the posting of a $100,000 bond."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (via Mr. Gowdey)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Cardinal case, this Court did say, in this case Cardinal properly invoked the original jurisdiction of a district court by way of its patent counterclaim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But you are giving arising under a different meaning for appellate purposes. You are including the counterclaim, a different meaning from original jurisdiction where, as Justice Breyer read, everybody agrees that for original jurisdiction purposes, counterclaims don't count."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gowdey",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOWDEY: There has not been a patent ruling"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gowdey",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOWDEY: If -- if you're looking at the claims that are pled at the pleading stage, the district court judge will know what appellate court will -- will apply certainly under the Aerojet rule, which -- which again would -- would place appellate jurisdiction at the Federal Circuit if you have a well-pled patent counterclaim coming in at the pleading stage as part of the defendant's answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dabney",
      "case_id": "2001-01-408",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kennedy, there is no difference between different interpretation and adaptation. The respondent's position would call for this Court to retreat from Christianson and to adopt some special interpretation of arising under unique to 1338(a) that deviates from the arising under language as it was clearly adopted by Congress in 1295."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
